WEBVTT - Clinical Vector: The Urgent Patient Referral Payload (English)

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Two-forty AM in a busy hospital emergency room. An urgent email arrives: 'Critical patient arriving in 15 minutes. Scans attached.'

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:45.000
In an emergency room, doctors and nurses open records immediately. Standard antivirus tools saw only a normal zip file.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:10.000
TraceXMail intercepted the file before anyone could double-click it. Examining the contents in a safe sandbox, it discovered a Trojan horse.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Disguised beneath a fake folder picture was a malicious program designed to lock all hospital patient files and demand a ransom.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:45.000
To a nurse, it looked like a medical file; to TraceXMail, it was a silent extortion weapon.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:02:10.000
At the same time, TraceXMail checked the server that sent the email against global law enforcement databases.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:30.000
The originating server was an exact match for a known international cybercrime syndicate that targets hospitals.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:50.000
TraceXMail destroyed the threat at the front door. The hospital’s medical equipment and patient charts stayed completely safe.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:03:05.000
When human lives are on the line, you cannot rely on guesswork. TraceXMail delivers real, understandable protection.
